  "conclusions": [
    "The PL/ARM implementation reproduces the locked Python equations closely; this proves implementation fidelity, not RF truth.",
    "Uncalibrated channel power was valid in all 30 independent records; worst absolute error was 0.188802 dB.",
    "Emission-center error reached 10.209 kHz in the tested BPSK records and carrier-line output abstained frequently.",
    "OBW was useful when the chosen analysis span contained the emission, but rectangular BPSK produced three false-valid narrow-span results with up to 325.644 kHz error.",
    "Therefore frequency/OBW/power computation is real and evidence-based, but full-emission span containment and live RF calibration remain acceptance gates.",
    "dBm stays unavailable until a measured, context-matched physical calibration profile exists."
